According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Natural Plastic-Free Chewing Gum market was valued at USD 121 million in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 231 million by 2032, growing at a CAGR of 9.7% during the forecast period (2024–2032). This growth is driven by increasing consumer awareness of environmental sustainability and the shift toward biodegradable alternatives to traditional chewing gum.
What is Natural Plastic-Free Chewing Gum?
Natural plastic-free chewing gum is an innovative product designed to address the environmental issues caused by traditional chewing gum. Conventional gum is typically made from synthetic rubber and polymers, which are non-biodegradable and contribute to environmental pollution. In contrast, plastic-free gum uses natural, biodegradable ingredients such as chicle (a natural latex harvested from the sapodilla tree), plant-based resins, and organic waxes, ensuring it breaks down naturally without harming ecosystems.
Leading brands in the market, including Chewsy, True Co., Chicza, Nuud Gum, Simply Gum, Glee Gum, Honest Gum, and Georganics, have pioneered sustainable gum formulations that appeal to eco-conscious consumers. Unlike traditional gum, which can take decades to decompose, plastic-free alternatives degrade within weeks to months, significantly reducing their environmental footprint.
